# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Secrets — the Gemini key must never reach the repo or the published site
.env

# Google service-account keys. .env only holds the PATH to one, so the key
# file itself needs its own rule or it ships with the repo. Deliberately NOT
# a blanket *.json — frontend/data/**.json is generated output that must be
# committed, or a fresh clone renders nothing.
secrets/
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
portfolio-*-*.json

# Everything generated: the formatted Excel reports, the pre-change snapshot
# store.backup() writes, and the JSON dump of the sheet taken before it was
# restructured. All of it is data, and the data lives in the Google Sheet —
# committing a copy would recreate exactly the second source of truth this
# repo no longer has.
backend/out/

# Gemini response cache. Purely a cost optimisation: the translations it
# produces are written into the IPO's YAML (the `i18n:` block) and those ARE
# committed, so a fresh clone renders every language without an API key.
backend/data/cache/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated at serve/deploy time from GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID. Not committed: the id
# lives in .env locally and in GitHub secrets for CI. It does become visible
# in the deployed site — the browser has to have it — but it stays out of the
# repo, and a fork points at its own sheet without editing tracked files.
frontend/js/config.js

# ── Notes and documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Working notes stay local. README.md is the one exception — it is the page
# anyone landing on the repo reads first, so it is tracked deliberately. The
# negation must come after the pattern that hides it; reversed, it does
# nothing.
*.md
!README.md

# Everything in docs/ is a working document, including the .docx builds and
# whatever else gets generated beside them.
#
# Written as `docs/*` rather than `docs/` on purpose: git does not descend
# into an excluded *directory*, so a bare `docs/` would make any later
# `!docs/…` line dead on arrival. Excluding the contents instead keeps that
# escape hatch open for the day one file in here does need tracking.
docs/*

# The exception the rule above was shaped to allow. This one is not a working
# document — it is the systems overview somebody reads to understand how the
# pipeline fits together, so it has to be visible in the repo and on GitHub
# rather than sitting on one machine's disk.
!docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.html
!docs/RUNNING.md

# Narration mirrored in from the "audio" Release by publish.yml, so the site
# can fetch it same-origin (Release assets send no CORS header — see cli.py
# _audio_base). Built on the runner every deploy; MP3s never belong in git.
frontend/audio/
